.TH AVR\-TESTS\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.4.1" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-tests-list \- List one page of test histories, grouped by test and configuration.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr tests list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List one page of test histories, grouped by test and configuration.
.PP
Counts describe each returned history window, not repository totals. Names appear when retained private detail is available; otherwise IDs are shown. Use --json '*' to retain status, pagination and repository context for agents.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (owner/name or rep-ID). Defaults to the git remote.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Defaults to the configured organization.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Rows per page (1-100). (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fITEXT\fR
Opaque next_cursor from the previous page. One page is read per invocation.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-tests (1),
.BR avr-tests-captures (1),
.BR avr-tests-history (1),
.BR avr-tests-status (1),
.BR avr-tests-view (1)
